Good morning! Let's get that reroll button fixed right away.

Why the Reroll Button Isn't Working
In Streamlit, when you click a button like st.button("🎲 Roll Alternative Option for this Scenario"), Streamlit re-runs the script from top to bottom. However, if the random seed or selection index isn't incrementing or changing state on each click, Streamlit will just regenerate the exact same random number and pull the exact same recipe every time.

To make the reroll button fully robust so it immediately shuffles to a different valid recipe every time you tap it, we need to track a reroll click counter in st.session_state.

The Fix for app.py
In your app.py file, find the section under Tab 1: Daily Briefing & Ops where the random choice is seeded and selected (around lines 650–670), and update it to this:

1. Add Session State Reroll Counter (Top of Tab 1)
Python
# Initialize session state tracker for daily briefing rerolls
if "reroll_counter" not in st.session_state:
  st.session_state.reroll_counter = 0
2. Update the Seeding & Random Choice Logic
Replace the static random seed block with one that factors in st.session_state.reroll_counter:

