To have an app appear in your Android App Drawer / App Listings (and in Settings -> Apps alongside regular installed apps) rather than just functioning as a pinned home-screen shortcut, Android must generate and register a WebAPK.

Chrome will only build and register a WebAPK in your system app listings when a website satisfies full PWA installation criteria. In Streamlit Cloud, the root HTML shell served by share.streamlit.io does not meet these criteria out of the box (it lacks an upfront top-level Web App Manifest and Service Worker in the initial server response), which is why Chrome creates a basic web shortcut instead of installing an actual system application.

