In the code snippet you shared, the indentation inside the string contains invisible non-breaking spaces (\xa0) introduced during copy-pasting from the web browser.

Python’s textwrap.dedent() only recognizes standard ASCII spaces ( ) and tabs (\t); it ignores non-breaking spaces. Because those leading spaces were not stripped, Markdown interpreted every line as an indented code block (the 4-space rule) and rendered raw HTML inside a <pre><code> block.

