Why It Scored 14/46 on PWABuilder
When PWABuilder tests a live URL, it evaluates the site against the official W3C Progressive Web App standards:

Missing Service Worker (-14 points): Streamlit Cloud does not register an offline Service Worker (sw.js) at the root domain.

Missing Canonical id & orientation (-6 points): The W3C specification requires an explicit unique application id (e.g. [https://cbrown-fragrance-ops.streamlit.app/?source=pwa](https://cbrown-fragrance-ops.streamlit.app/?source=pwa)) and a locked orientation: "portrait".

Missing Multi-Resolution Icon Set (-12 points): PWABuilder requires both a 512x512 maskable icon and a 192x192 standard icon declared in the manifest.

When PWABuilder scans *.streamlit.app, it only reads Streamlit’s generic fallback headers (granting only 14 points for basic HTTPS and a generic title).

